-/* =========================================================
-   ALEXANDER WATSON STUDIO — VISUAL SYSTEM
-   Final authority for surfaces, spacing, cards, labels and actions.
-   ========================================================= */
-
-/* Newsreader replaces Instrument Serif as the heading face.
-
-   Instrument Serif ships a single weight. Every heading on the site was
-   therefore 400, and hierarchy had to be carried by size alone — which is
-   why the scale had drifted into two hundred and thirty-eight separate
-   font-size declarations. Newsreader is a variable text serif with a
-   200-800 weight axis, so a heading can be distinguished by weight as well
-   as size, and a small heading can hold its own without being enlarged.
-
-   It is also the face named in the studio's own Brand & Digital Identity
-   Guidelines v1.1, which the website had not yet followed: the site and the
-   client-facing documents are now one system rather than two.
-
-   SIL Open Font License, self-hosted (assets/fonts/OFL-Newsreader.txt).
-   One 58KB variable file, latin subset — smaller than the pair it replaces
-   plus the weights it would otherwise have needed. No external request,
-   which matters: netlify.toml sets font-src 'self'. */
-@font-face {
-  font-family: "Newsreader";
-  font-style: normal;
-  font-weight: 200 800;
-  font-display: swap;
-  src: url("/assets/fonts/newsreader-latin-wght-normal.woff2") format("woff2");
-}
